<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  BTDGravshipQuest_GrammarFix.xml            Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-13
  ============================================================================

  THE GOAL
  ========
  The [BTD] Gravship Blueprints "Downed Gravship" quest renders with NO
  DESCRIPTION AT ALL. Fix is one string: drop the author's credit line out of
  the quest description, because RimWorld's grammar resolver reads it as a rule
  reference and fails the whole node.

  This is gravship content, and the gravship is the one thing v1 ships DEEP —
  a scavenger clan looting a crashed hull is exactly the campaign's premise.
  So the quest is wanted; only its description is broken.

  WHY IT IS NEEDED  [MEASURED 2026-08-13, from the live Player.log + the def]
  ==========================================================================
  Source of truth, read directly:

    .../workshop/content/294100/3575162262/1.6/Defs/QuestScriptDefs/
      Script_BTD_DownedGravship.xml:13-19

      <questDescriptionRules>
        <rulesStrings>
          <li>questDescription->A damaged gravship has crash-landed nearby. ...

    [BTD] Gravship Blueprints Quest</li>          ← the credit line
        </rulesStrings>
      </questDescriptionRules>

  In RimWorld's grammar, SQUARE BRACKETS ARE A SYMBOL REFERENCE. `[BTD]` is
  therefore read as "resolve the rule named BTD", which does not exist. A rule
  string containing ONE unresolvable symbol fails ENTIRELY — it does not
  degrade to plain text. The whole questDescription is discarded.

  Verbatim from `Player.log`, the 17:30-21:10 session (1 occurrence):

      Grammar unresolvable. Root 'questDescription'
      GRAMMAR RESOLUTION TRACE
      1  questDescription -> A damaged gravship has crash-landed nearby. ...
                             [BTD] Gravship Blueprints Quest
           BTD -> UNRESOLVABLE
         questDescription -> UNRESOLVABLE
      CONSTANTS
      BTD_DownedGravship_exists              True
      sitePart                               BTD_DownedGravship

  Note the trace confirms the site part resolved fine — the quest FIRES and is
  playable. Only its description is empty. The mod is not broken; one line is.

  PLAYER-VISIBLE?  YES, and that is why this is worth a patch at all.
  ===================================================================
  `<autoAccept>true</autoAccept>` on this def means the quest is accepted
  without the player opening a dialog, so the description is read in the Quests
  tab AFTER the fact — which is precisely when a player wants to know what the
  site is and that it expires in 30 days. An empty description there reads as a
  broken mod, not as a stylistic choice.

  WHY REPLACE AND NOT REMOVE
  ==========================
  Removing `questDescriptionRules` outright would leave the quest with no
  description by a different route. We want the author's TEXT, minus the four
  characters that break it. The credit is preserved in the mod's About.xml and
  README.txt, which is where a credit belongs and where it renders correctly.

  UPSTREAM, NOT OURS
  ==================
  This is a defect in `3575162262`, not in anything we authored. Reported here
  rather than fixed at source because editing a Workshop mod in place is undone
  by the next Steam update or validate.

  GUARDED, and the guard is the point
  ===================================
  Wrapped in `PatchOperationFindMod` on the mod's NAME (`[BTD] Gravship
  Blueprints`, packageId `btd.remix.gravshipblueprints`, ws `3575162262`) —
  read from its About.xml, not guessed. Without the guard an unmatched
  PatchOperationReplace throws a RED ERROR on every launch, which is a worse
  outcome than the bug it fixes: the quest description is cosmetic, a red error
  is noise in every future triage. Two ways this becomes unmatched — the owner
  unsubscribes the mod, or the author fixes the credit line upstream and our
  xpath finds a node we already changed.

  ⚠️ `FindMod` matches the mod NAME, not the packageId, and this one begins
  with a literal square bracket. That is fine in XML text and is NOT the
  grammar-symbol problem being fixed here — the resolver only reads brackets
  inside rule strings.

  SUCCESS LOOKS LIKE
  ==================
  POSITIVE observation, not a clean log: the Downed Gravship quest shows its
  description text in the Quests tab. The negative half is that
  `Grammar unresolvable. Root 'questDescription'` stops appearing — but on its
  own that proves nothing, because the quest may simply not have fired.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>[BTD] Gravship Blueprints</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/QuestScriptDef[defName="BTD_DownedGravship"]/questDescriptionRules/rulesStrings</xpath>
      <value>
        <rulesStrings>
          <li>questDescription->A damaged gravship has crash-landed nearby. Hostile forces are defending the wreck. Hack the damaged grav engine and loot what you can before the site expires in 30 days.</li>
        </rulesStrings>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
